## Native Runtime Libraries for Precompiled Python Wheels

Precompiled Android wheels (PEP 738 tags such as `android_24_arm64_v8a`,
served by community indexes configured in `pip.conf`) link against shared
libraries from the Termux distribution. The libraries below are shipped inside
the APK (`feature-python/src/main/jniLibs/`) and are loaded only when a Python
package that requires them is imported.

| Library | License |
|---------|---------|
| libopenblas.so (OpenBLAS) | BSD-3-Clause |
| libc++_shared.so (LLVM libc++) | Apache 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions — provided by the NDK `c++_shared` STL, do not duplicate it in `jniLibs` |
| libandroid-support.so (Termux) | See https://github.com/termux/termux-packages |
| libz.so.1 (zlib) | zlib License |
| libbz2.so.1.0 (bzip2) | BSD-style (bzip2 License) |
| liblzma.so.5 (XZ Utils) | 0BSD / public domain |
| libzstd.so.1 (Zstandard) | BSD-3-Clause (dual-licensed, used under BSD) |
| libpng16.so (libpng) | PNG Reference Library License (zlib-style) |
| libfreetype.so (FreeType) | FreeType License (FTL) |
| libjpeg.so.8 (libjpeg-turbo) | BSD-3-Clause / IJG |
| libtiff.so (libtiff) | libtiff License (MIT-style) |
| libwebp.so, libwebpmux.so, libwebpdemux.so, libsharpyuv.so (libwebp 1.5.0, rebuilt from upstream sources with `-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384` for 16KB page devices) | BSD-3-Clause |
| libopenjp2.so (OpenJPEG) | BSD-2-Clause |
| liblcms2.so (Little CMS) | MIT |
| libxcb.so, libXau.so, libXdmcp.so | MIT |
| libraqm.so | MIT |
| libharfbuzz.so (HarfBuzz) | MIT (Old MIT) |
| libgraphite2.so (Graphite2) | LGPL-2.1-or-later / MPL-1.1 |
| libglib-2.0.so.0 (GLib) | LGPL-2.1-or-later |
| libfribidi.so (FriBidi) | LGPL-2.1-or-later |
| libpcre2-8.so (PCRE2) | BSD-3-Clause |
| libxml2.so.16, libxslt.so, libexslt.so | MIT |
| libyaml-0.so (libyaml) | MIT |
| libffi.so (libffi) | MIT |
| liblz4.so (LZ4) | BSD-2-Clause |
| libsodium.so (libsodium) | ISC |
| libzmq.so (ZeroMQ / libzmq) | MPL-2.0 |
| libbrotlicommon.so, libbrotlidec.so (Brotli) | MIT |
| libsqlite3.so, libsqlite3.so.0 (SQLite) | Public domain (SQLite Blessing) |
| libcrypto_python.so, libssl_python.so (OpenSSL built for CPython, renamed so it cannot clash with the OpenSSL shipped for git) | Apache-2.0 |
| libpython3.14.so, libpython3.so, libpython_exe.so (CPython interpreter) | Python Software Foundation License 2.0 |

`libiconv.so` and `libpcre2-8.so` are already provided by the bundled git
binaries in the terminal module and are therefore not duplicated here.

Libraries whose upstream file name carries a version suffix (`libz.so.1`,
`libbz2.so.1.0`, `liblzma.so.5`, `libzstd.so.1`, `libjpeg.so.8`,
`libxml2.so.16`, `libglib-2.0.so.0`, `libsqlite3.so.0`) cannot be packaged by
AGP, so they are shipped as assets under
`feature-python/src/main/assets/nativelibs/<abi>/` and unpacked into
`$PYTHONHOME/lib` on first launch.

**GPL-3.0 notice:** `libimagequant.so` (pngquant) is required by Pillow's core
`_imaging` extension and is dual-licensed under **GPL-3.0-or-later** or a
commercial license. Bundling it in an Apache-2.0 application requires either
accepting GPL-3.0 for the combined work or obtaining a commercial license from
pngquant. Remove `libimagequant.so` from `jniLibs` if this is not acceptable —
Pillow will then fail to import, which is the trade-off.

